*****************************************************************************
                     deepstream-kitti-overlay
                             README
*****************************************************************************

===============================================================================
1. Prerequisites:
===============================================================================

Please follow instructions in the apps/sample_apps/deepstream-app/README on how
to install the prerequisites for the DeepStream SDK, the DeepStream SDK itself,
and the apps.

You must have the following development packages installed
   GStreamer-1.0
   GStreamer-1.0 Base Plugins

To install these packages, execute the following command:
   sudo apt-get install libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev libgstreamer1.0-dev


===============================================================================
2. Purpose:
===============================================================================

This sample does NOT run inference. It overlays bounding boxes from
pre-generated DeepStream KITTI dump files onto one or more video sources for
offline analysis.

It builds on deepstream-test3 to demonstrate how to:

* Use multiple sources in the pipeline.
* Use a uridecodebin so that any type of input (e.g. RTSP/File), any GStreamer
  supported container format, and any codec can be used as input.
* Attach already generated KITTI data (inferred object information per frame)
  to the source video.
* Access buffers using appsink APIs for use outside GStreamer.

Pipeline overview:
  uridecodebin (per source) -> nvstreammux -> nvmultistreamtiler ->
  nvvideoconvert -> nvdsosd -> display / filesink (+ appsink branch)

KITTI metadata is attached in a pad probe before OSD, so boxes are drawn by
nvdsosd from the dump files rather than from a live PGIE.


===============================================================================
3. To compile:
===============================================================================

  $ cd src/apps/sample_apps/deepstream-kitti-overlay
  $ Set CUDA_VER in the Makefile as per platform.
      For x86 & Jetson, CUDA_VER=13.2
  $ sudo make CUDA_VER=13.2
    (sudo not required in Docker containers)

NOTE: To compile the sources, run make with "sudo" or root permission when
installing into system paths.


===============================================================================
4. End-to-end steps to run:
===============================================================================

This app requires a KITTI dump directory produced by deepstream-app for the
SAME video URI(s) you will overlay. Dump files are named:

  <ctx>_<stream>_<frame>.txt
  e.g. 00_000_000000.txt, 00_000_000001.txt, ...

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step A — Generate KITTI dumps with deepstream-app
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1) Pick a deepstream-app config (example uses the shipped 4-source sample):

     /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/configs/deepstream-app/

2) In the [application] section, set (or uncomment) an absolute output directory:

     [application]
     gie-kitti-output-dir=/tmp/kitti_data1

   Create the directory first:

     $ mkdir -p /tmp/kitti_data1

3) Ensure the config URI matches the video you will later pass to this overlay
   app. Example:

     [source0]
     uri=file:///opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/streams/sample_1080p_h264.mp4

4) Run deepstream-app from the config directory (relative model/stream paths
   resolve from cwd):

     $ cd /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/configs/deepstream-app
     $ deepstream-app -c source4_1080p_dec_infer-resnet_tracker_sgie_tiled_display.txt

5) Verify dumps were written:

     $ ls /tmp/kitti_data1 | head
     # expect: 00_000_000000.txt 00_000_000001.txt ...

NOTE: For multi-source deepstream-app runs, dumps for all streams typically
land in the same gie-kitti-output-dir with different stream IDs in the
filename. For this overlay app, pass one URI + one kitti directory pair per
source. Prefer generating one dump directory per source when overlaying
multiple inputs.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step B — Run deepstream-kitti-overlay
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Always run from this sample directory (or use absolute paths for kitti dirs):

  $ cd src/apps/sample_apps/deepstream-kitti-overlay

Arguments are URI / kitti-dir pairs:

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay <uri1> <kitti1> [uri2] <kitti2> ... [uriN] <kittiN>

Display output (single source):

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay \
      file:///opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/streams/sample_1080p_h264.mp4 \
      /tmp/kitti_data1

Display output (two sources):

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay \
      file:///path/to/video1.mp4 /tmp/kitti_data1 \
      file:///path/to/video2.mp4 /tmp/kitti_data2

RTSP example:

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay \
      rtsp://127.0.0.1/video1 /tmp/kitti_data1 \
      rtsp://127.0.0.1/video2 /tmp/kitti_data2

Save overlayed output to an MP4 (hardware encoder):

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay \
      file:///opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/streams/sample_1080p_h264.mp4 \
      /tmp/kitti_data1 \
      outfile-hw-enc /tmp/out.mp4

Software encoder (e.g. Ampere platforms if HW encode is unavailable):

  $ ./deepstream-kitti-overlay \
      file:///opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream-9.1/samples/streams/sample_1080p_h264.mp4 \
      /tmp/kitti_data1 \
      outfile-sw-enc /tmp/out.mp4


===============================================================================
5. Notes / common failures:
===============================================================================

* The third (and later odd) arguments must be directories of KITTI dump files,
  not a single video path and not an empty folder.
* Use absolute paths for kitti directories when possible.
* The video URI used for overlay should match the stream that produced the
  dumps (same content / frame count). Mismatched frame numbers are reported
  at runtime and boxes may not align.
* Non-KITTI files in the dump directory are skipped; if no valid
  <ctx>_<stream>_<frame>.txt files are present, the app exits with
  "Empty Kitti Directory Provided".
* outfile-hw-enc / outfile-sw-enc require a .mp4 output filename.

Refer to the deepstream-test3 sample documentation for an example of simple
multi-stream inference, bounding-box overlay, and rendering.
